WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.409
Telo Ride opens fast. The first load is ninety kilobytes, gzipped.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.429
After every build, a check gzips exactly what the first screen downloads, and fails

00:00:15.429 --> 00:00:16.959
above three hundred.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.022
The raw budget is tight: it warns at three oh two, and fails at three oh five.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:41.202
The 3D world waits for the race. Home carries no Three.js at all.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:52.042
Home's first load, from a phone to the full screen.

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:03.748
What the tests prove: a light first load, and the world only when you ride.

00:01:09.685 --> 00:01:14.288
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:14.633 --> 00:01:19.145
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:20.816
every hill and interval.

00:01:21.161 --> 00:01:26.339
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:26.339 --> 00:01:31.787
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:31.787 --> 00:01:34.777
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:35.123 --> 00:01:37.615
A custom workout lives under Profile.
